00:37:17.220 --> 00:37:22.220
but my husband I came back to Tennessee

00:37:25.060 --> 00:37:30.060
and just a few weeks into being back,

00:37:32.730 --> 00:37:37.230
met the man that I married.

00:37:37.230 --> 00:37:42.090
We've been married 11 years
and now currently presently

00:37:44.220 --> 00:37:45.823
and for the last few years,

00:37:47.975 --> 00:37:49.430
well he always has worn overalls

00:37:49.430 --> 00:37:51.023
and he's a giant man.

00:37:51.910 --> 00:37:55.640
The only difference is he's
brown and my Pepo wasn't

00:37:58.350 --> 00:38:01.163
but he's got the long gray beard now,

00:38:02.575 --> 00:38:04.313
he's 27 years older than me.

00:38:06.033 --> 00:38:08.573
I didn't care then I thought,

00:38:10.060 --> 00:38:11.833
I did think he was beautiful.

00:38:14.750 --> 00:38:18.237
He didn't look his age
and I wanted stability

00:38:21.970 --> 00:38:23.233
and I wanted normal.

00:38:26.406 --> 00:38:28.106
And for a little while I had that.

00:38:28.950 --> 00:38:33.013
So I do see, I guess like,
like a tie between the two

00:38:36.630 --> 00:38:38.173
they're very much the same.

00:38:39.023 --> 00:38:40.590
The overalls, the gray beards,

00:38:40.590 --> 00:38:44.623
the narcissistic bullshit.

00:38:49.180 --> 00:38:51.290
In a lot of ways, they're the same person.

00:38:51.290 --> 00:38:55.460
And I think the fact that
neither of them liked each other

00:38:55.460 --> 00:39:00.460
from the beginning probably
should have been a big red flag.

00:39:02.750 --> 00:39:07.453
We let him, it gets sicker, I get sicker.

00:39:09.200 --> 00:39:12.020
I left Oklahoma and you would think

00:39:12.020 --> 00:39:14.000
that I would have never looked back

00:39:14.000 --> 00:39:19.000
but he came to Tennessee
when I was pregnant with,

00:39:21.690 --> 00:39:25.620
I didn't know it was a girl
yet, but my second child

00:39:26.870 --> 00:39:31.273
and I was with my husband he
stayed with us for one night.

00:39:32.559 --> 00:39:34.209
It was supposed to be a few days.

00:39:36.465 --> 00:39:38.550
And he sang a song right
in front of my husband

00:39:38.550 --> 00:39:43.550
about one he had written about
a girl with long black hair

00:39:43.900 --> 00:39:47.180
and green eyes kissing
her under some trees

00:39:47.180 --> 00:39:51.243
in a like back creek or some stupid shit.

00:39:52.124 --> 00:39:54.240
And my husband wasn't stupid.

00:39:54.240 --> 00:39:55.990
He picked up on it quickly.

00:39:55.990 --> 00:39:59.807
And the straw that broke the camel's back

00:40:03.150 --> 00:40:06.210
was the next day he walked in, my husband.

00:40:06.210 --> 00:40:08.193
I was there alone with my grandfather.

00:40:09.410 --> 00:40:12.090
He, my grandfather, never tried anything

00:40:12.090 --> 00:40:15.203
during that trip in Tennessee
when he came to see us.

00:40:16.390 --> 00:40:19.570
But I was sitting at the
kitchen table doing something.

00:40:19.570 --> 00:40:22.340
And right when my husband opened the door,

00:40:22.340 --> 00:40:25.610
my grandfather walked up
behind me and he put his hand

00:40:25.610 --> 00:40:30.200
around the back of my
neck and he leaned down

00:40:30.200 --> 00:40:33.837
and I didn't realize I was
making a face, but I guess I did.

00:40:33.837 --> 00:40:37.590
And my husband saw it and he pulled me

00:40:37.590 --> 00:40:39.670
in the back bedroom and
he said, "What's going on?

00:40:39.670 --> 00:40:40.810
Something's going on."

00:40:40.810 --> 00:40:42.143
And I told him nothing.

00:40:44.110 --> 00:40:46.910
I just didn't want to be
there if he was there.

00:40:46.910 --> 00:40:51.910
So long story short, Pepo left that day

00:40:52.850 --> 00:40:56.000
and I never saw him again

00:40:56.000 --> 00:40:59.010
because I went on to find
out a couple months later

00:40:59.010 --> 00:41:02.400
that I was carrying a girl and

00:41:14.270 --> 00:41:15.603
not my kids.

00:41:21.270 --> 00:41:22.893
Then I had another little girl.

00:41:25.660 --> 00:41:27.923
I never spoke to him
through all these years.

00:41:30.620 --> 00:41:35.150
And then three years ago I
got subpoenaed to testify

00:41:37.200 --> 00:41:38.837
for my baby cousin against him.

00:41:38.837 --> 00:41:41.087
And I was pregnant with
my third little girl.

00:41:44.900 --> 00:41:47.640
All of us came from all over the country

00:41:47.640 --> 00:41:49.510
to testify against him.

00:41:49.510 --> 00:41:54.510
And I was the only one on the stand.

00:41:55.870 --> 00:41:58.140
The defense attorney asked me how I felt

00:41:58.140 --> 00:41:59.247
about being there that day.

00:41:59.247 --> 00:42:04.113
And I said horrible, because
I loved him very much

00:42:06.770 --> 00:42:10.240
and I didn't want to see
him put away in prison

00:42:10.240 --> 00:42:15.240
and hurt because I felt like
he was just a very sick man.

00:42:17.670 --> 00:42:20.090
Especially given the
conversations that we had had

00:42:20.090 --> 00:42:23.763
about why he thought he
didn't things that he did.

00:42:25.610 --> 00:42:28.917
I testified against him
because I loved my baby cousin

00:42:28.917 --> 00:42:32.330
and his potential future
victims more than him

00:42:32.330 --> 00:42:35.823
but I still loved him.

00:42:37.035 --> 00:42:39.735
And I didn't want to see
anything awful happen to him.

00:42:43.770 --> 00:42:48.770
I don't love him now. He was convicted.

00:42:50.090 --> 00:42:54.210
He got seven years for what he did to her.

00:42:54.210 --> 00:42:58.373
And he died after only
two years in prison.

00:42:59.890 --> 00:43:03.280
He actually died a couple of weeks

00:43:03.280 --> 00:43:08.060
before I had already gone
through all the loops.

00:43:08.060 --> 00:43:11.520
I had to go through all the hoops

00:43:11.520 --> 00:43:14.823
I had to jump through to go see him.

00:43:18.039 --> 00:43:21.950
Being a victim they don't
generally let you have a visit

00:43:21.950 --> 00:43:24.270
with the perpetrator in Oklahoma

00:43:24.270 --> 00:43:26.300
but I wanted him to see me now

00:43:26.300 --> 00:43:30.480
and see that, I knew
that he accepted my visit

00:43:30.480 --> 00:43:32.380
when he denied everybody else's

00:43:32.380 --> 00:43:34.080
because he thought he could still

00:43:37.690 --> 00:43:39.620
play one last game maybe,

00:43:39.620 --> 00:43:42.933
but I needed him to see that I'm probably

00:43:46.080 --> 00:43:49.856
still pretty sick in the
head, but I'm not his anymore.

00:43:49.856 --> 00:43:53.703
And I'm not under his spell anymore.

00:43:55.610 --> 00:44:00.610
And also tell him that I love him

00:44:00.837 --> 00:44:01.863
and I forgive him.

00:44:03.570 --> 00:44:05.463
I love the good in him.

00:44:07.405 --> 00:44:08.890
And I forgive the bad in him

00:44:08.890 --> 00:44:11.750
that hurt me so bad and
the people I love so bad

00:44:12.630 --> 00:44:14.593
but I never got that chance.

00:44:17.560 --> 00:44:22.093
He died before I could go, so...

00:44:37.550 --> 00:44:39.710
- [Mark] This was how many years ago?

00:44:39.710 --> 00:44:43.893
- [Star] He died in
December almost a year ago.

00:44:50.200 --> 00:44:51.660
- [Mark] So it's still fairly fresh.

00:44:51.660 --> 00:44:54.890
- Yeah, been disowned by his whole family,

00:44:54.890 --> 00:44:57.983
except for two cousins.

00:45:04.540 --> 00:45:08.850
They're all very angry
with us, for testifying.

00:45:08.850 --> 00:45:12.050
And they're all very, very angry,

00:45:12.050 --> 00:45:16.473
that myself and my aunt speak about it.

00:45:24.258 --> 00:45:27.463
Cause like I said, he
was super charismatic

00:45:27.463 --> 00:45:30.610
and nobody could really believe

00:45:30.610 --> 00:45:33.397
that he was capable of
the things that he did.

00:45:33.397 --> 00:45:36.980
But I guess I need, I
need to make it clear

00:45:40.300 --> 00:45:42.630
that I understand that
there's a big difference

00:45:42.630 --> 00:45:46.213
in what he did to all of us as children

00:45:51.670 --> 00:45:53.760
especially what he did to my baby cousin,

00:45:53.760 --> 00:45:55.860
my aunts and my mother.

00:45:55.860 --> 00:46:00.500
And then what happened
when I was an adult.

00:46:00.500 --> 00:46:03.767
And I guess that's why I'm
here today because nobody,

00:46:08.290 --> 00:46:12.813
it's a lot easier to say
that things were done

00:46:14.410 --> 00:46:16.226
to you when you were an innocent child

00:46:16.226 --> 00:46:20.260
and you couldn't fight back or say no

00:46:22.450 --> 00:46:25.140
but as an adult at any age,

00:46:25.140 --> 00:46:27.773
when you can and you just don't,

00:46:29.910 --> 00:46:32.683
there's like a huge
amount of like self hate

00:46:35.300 --> 00:46:36.760
and guilt that comes with that.

00:46:36.760 --> 00:46:41.760
And it's damn near taking
me out a couple of times.

00:46:45.910 --> 00:46:50.910
So like court, the D.A. told
me that this is so common

00:46:51.268 --> 00:46:56.268
that she hears about it so often.

00:46:56.280 --> 00:46:58.270
I had to take her in a
back room and tell her,

00:46:58.270 --> 00:47:02.450
look just in case I don't want
a curve ball thrown at you.

00:47:02.450 --> 00:47:07.110
And my cousin's whole
case get blown wide open

00:47:07.110 --> 00:47:10.560
in case he decides to say
that this happened between us.

00:47:10.560 --> 00:47:14.610
And she said this happens all the times.

00:47:14.610 --> 00:47:17.570
So if it happens all the time,

00:47:17.570 --> 00:47:21.420
that's news to me because I
never hear people talk about it.

00:47:21.420 --> 00:47:26.420
And well, I think it
needs to be talked about

00:47:27.141 --> 00:47:27.974
because it does happen,

00:47:27.974 --> 00:47:31.070
especially here in the mountains, anyway.

00:47:37.153 --> 00:47:39.683
I do feel responsible for my part in it?

00:47:42.040 --> 00:47:44.950
But I also feel like people like him

00:47:44.950 --> 00:47:47.460
are really good at what they do and

00:47:50.740 --> 00:47:54.563
I know the guilt that I live with,

00:47:58.590 --> 00:48:00.660
there's gotta be so many
other people out there

00:48:00.660 --> 00:48:01.923
living with the same.

00:48:04.610 --> 00:48:06.409
And I guess my hope, like,

00:48:06.409 --> 00:48:10.823
what I hope for with this interview,

00:48:13.260 --> 00:48:15.910
is maybe start a conversation about it

00:48:15.910 --> 00:48:19.843
where it's not so taboo to talk about.

00:48:23.517 --> 00:48:28.517
Maybe people like me
reach out for help sooner.

00:48:30.120 --> 00:48:35.120
And I also hope that maybe it would

00:48:44.120 --> 00:48:45.940
set me free 'cause

00:48:52.100 --> 00:48:54.566
he's gone, but I'm not.

00:48:54.566 --> 00:48:58.433
And it's all still here and very real.

00:49:08.370 --> 00:49:11.630
- [Mark] So you were having
sex with your grandfather,

00:49:11.630 --> 00:49:13.610
who was also at one point having sex

00:49:13.610 --> 00:49:15.290
with your mom, his daughter?

00:49:15.290 --> 00:49:16.870
- Yes, but I need to make it clear

00:49:16.870 --> 00:49:21.860
that that was actual, honest to God, rape.

00:49:21.860 --> 00:49:24.900
Like she fought back and said no.

00:49:24.900 --> 00:49:27.860
The last time that he
raped her, she was 16,

00:49:27.860 --> 00:49:29.970
which is when she fell pregnant with me.

00:49:29.970 --> 00:49:34.970
And for much of my life,
she told me when I was,

00:49:39.670 --> 00:49:42.730
I want to say I was about 15 or 16

00:49:42.730 --> 00:49:45.420
that he could be my biological father

00:49:48.908 --> 00:49:51.703
and I lived in horror of that fact

00:49:56.120 --> 00:50:00.790
which also kind of, I don't know,

00:50:00.790 --> 00:50:04.777
if catch 22 is the right
word, but it felt disgusting.

00:50:07.330 --> 00:50:09.133
But at the same time I thought,

00:50:11.320 --> 00:50:13.620
anybody but my dad at the time,

00:50:13.620 --> 00:50:15.110
you know, I was an angry teenager.

00:50:15.110 --> 00:50:17.760
And I thought, even if it has to be

00:50:17.760 --> 00:50:20.190
this funky old backwards bullshit,

00:50:20.190 --> 00:50:23.140
at least I have maybe a shot

00:50:23.140 --> 00:50:25.810
at a dad that loves me
and says he loves me

00:50:25.810 --> 00:50:30.630
and tells me I'm beautiful
and et cetera, et cetera.

00:50:30.630 --> 00:50:33.590
And then whenever I moved to Oklahoma

00:50:33.590 --> 00:50:37.130
and I asked him about this, his take on it

00:50:37.130 --> 00:50:40.360
was that it was consensual
sex in the back of his van.

00:50:40.360 --> 00:50:43.970
Even though my mother was
16, his biological daughter.

00:50:43.970 --> 00:50:46.890
And yes we know for sure it's biological,

00:50:46.890 --> 00:50:50.720
'cause we've, my mom and I
both taken a 23andMe test

00:50:52.491 --> 00:50:55.033
and many of his family
members are on there.

00:50:56.610 --> 00:50:59.870
He said that it was consensual

00:50:59.870 --> 00:51:03.170
and he went into graphic
detail about what happened.

00:51:03.170 --> 00:51:05.340
And then he scoffed

00:51:05.340 --> 00:51:08.140
and he giggled and he
said, "That's ridiculous.

00:51:08.140 --> 00:51:10.983
I had a vasectomy after
your aunt was born.

00:51:12.493 --> 00:51:15.120
I never could have been your father."

00:51:15.120 --> 00:51:19.027
And then I remember also
probably several weeks

00:51:22.150 --> 00:51:27.150
into what do you call it?

00:51:28.130 --> 00:51:29.883
Our sexual shit,

00:51:35.550 --> 00:51:40.550
him saying that he would love nothing more

00:51:40.830 --> 00:51:45.830
than to be able to come
back home to East Tennessee

00:51:46.800 --> 00:51:48.610
and live in a cabin with me

00:51:48.610 --> 00:51:53.610
and have babies and spend
the rest of his life

00:51:54.280 --> 00:51:55.740
living like a mountain man.

00:51:55.740 --> 00:51:59.520
Like he was meant to be,
which was all a facade.

00:51:59.520 --> 00:52:02.360
He played this mountain
man character in Oklahoma

00:52:02.360 --> 00:52:07.360
but he wasn't, he was
from a moderately big city

00:52:09.530 --> 00:52:13.770
and the straw hat and the
cowboy boots and the overalls

00:52:13.770 --> 00:52:18.770
were all just a bullshit
character he played.

00:52:20.420 --> 00:52:24.700
But yeah, there was
something really broken

00:52:24.700 --> 00:52:26.563
and really sick inside him.

00:52:33.840 --> 00:52:36.210
Thank God he did have a vasectomy

00:52:36.210 --> 00:52:39.410
or he probably would have been my father

00:52:39.410 --> 00:52:44.410
and I probably would have
had at least one of his kids,

00:52:46.590 --> 00:52:48.243
just being honest.

00:52:54.190 --> 00:52:55.023
- [Mark] If you're 20 years old,

00:52:55.023 --> 00:52:57.140
how do you let your
grandfather get away with this?

00:52:57.140 --> 00:52:58.190
How does this happen?

00:52:59.260 --> 00:53:01.510
It seems like you'd be old
enough to protect yourself.

00:53:01.510 --> 00:53:06.510
- I was, and I don't have like a black

00:53:06.740 --> 00:53:07.700
and white answer for that.

00:53:07.700 --> 00:53:11.040
But I think it was like
a multitude of things.

00:53:11.040 --> 00:53:15.917
Number one, it was the memories of him.

00:53:17.340 --> 00:53:20.360
So only had a couple of bad
ones, but the rest were good.

00:53:20.360 --> 00:53:22.877
The memories of this big
giant Santa Claus, Pepo,

00:53:22.877 --> 00:53:24.370
all that played the guitar.

00:53:24.370 --> 00:53:26.370
And he'd sing this sneaky snake song.

00:53:26.370 --> 00:53:29.769
And like everybody wanted
a Pepo like that, right.

00:53:29.769 --> 00:53:33.450
And then my mom spending years telling us

00:53:33.450 --> 00:53:36.180
no, no, no, no, no,
you can't talk to them.

00:53:36.180 --> 00:53:39.360
We'll like I said, I
was rebellious as shit.

00:53:39.360 --> 00:53:43.720
So of course I'm going to
do the opposite, right?

00:53:43.720 --> 00:53:45.437
Not realizing how dangerous it was

00:53:45.437 --> 00:53:47.973
and why she was saying no, no, no, no, no.

00:53:50.270 --> 00:53:55.270
Then I think that being with my father

00:53:56.290 --> 00:54:00.180
and I'm not trying to
bash him by saying this,

00:54:00.180 --> 00:54:02.583
but being with my father
for so many years,

00:54:05.910 --> 00:54:07.210
if I hadn't have lived with him,

00:54:07.210 --> 00:54:09.470
I think it would have definitely
gone down differently.

00:54:09.470 --> 00:54:14.470
But six years of 12 to 18,

00:54:17.430 --> 00:54:19.630
some of the most formative
years in my life,

00:54:22.867 --> 00:54:27.490
I was taught every day that
I had to submit or else,

00:54:27.490 --> 00:54:30.150
and that I didn't have a choice.

00:54:30.150 --> 00:54:35.150
And having a male figure's
will imposed on me

00:54:38.170 --> 00:54:40.600
and it was just a fucking way of life.

00:54:40.600 --> 00:54:43.310
It just was how it was.

00:54:43.310 --> 00:54:46.270
And then add on to that
the four-year boyfriend

00:54:46.270 --> 00:54:47.860
and it was the same shit.

00:54:47.860 --> 00:54:52.860
And there was nobody in this world,

00:54:53.700 --> 00:54:54.533
I wouldn't fight.

00:54:54.533 --> 00:54:57.710
In fact, I stayed in trouble
constantly in school and out

00:54:57.710 --> 00:55:00.530
for fighting, usually females.

00:55:00.530 --> 00:55:03.570
But when it came to men,

00:55:03.570 --> 00:55:07.973
even if I had to fight
them, I still in the end,

00:55:09.340 --> 00:55:12.250
ended up submitting and
doing what they wanted.

00:55:12.250 --> 00:55:15.030
So by the time I got to him,

00:55:15.030 --> 00:55:17.060
I've gone through all
these years of conditioning

00:55:17.060 --> 00:55:20.134
from my father and this shit boyfriend,

00:55:20.134 --> 00:55:25.134
and then the learning how to,

00:55:26.860 --> 00:55:29.373
I guess the word is disassociate,

00:55:31.000 --> 00:55:34.223
through my drug years or year-ish,

00:55:37.580 --> 00:55:40.440
sleeping with strangers,
old men, whatever.

00:55:40.440 --> 00:55:45.440
So by the time I got to him,
he was like the ultimate.

00:55:46.210 --> 00:55:48.430
He was physically the biggest

00:55:48.430 --> 00:55:51.080
and personality-wise the biggest.

00:55:51.080 --> 00:55:55.010
And he had the biggest
presence and the strongest will

00:55:55.010 --> 00:55:57.453
and it was almost like being,

00:56:00.170 --> 00:56:02.140
hypnotized is not the right word,

00:56:02.140 --> 00:56:04.793
but there was no saying no.

00:56:05.690 --> 00:56:08.920
It just never really crossed
my mind as an option.

00:56:08.920 --> 00:56:10.770
And even when it ended,

00:56:10.770 --> 00:56:15.770
it wasn't like I found the
courage to do it myself.

00:56:16.200 --> 00:56:18.370
I got very, very sick
and was in the hospital

00:56:18.370 --> 00:56:22.750
for over a week and they didn't
think I was gonna make it.

00:56:22.750 --> 00:56:25.620
So my paternal grandparents drove

00:56:25.620 --> 00:56:27.710
from Tennessee to Oklahoma

00:56:27.710 --> 00:56:31.230
and I miraculously started to get better.

00:56:31.230 --> 00:56:33.610
And once I got better, they asked me

00:56:34.900 --> 00:56:37.660
I reckon they got tired
of being angry with me

00:56:37.660 --> 00:56:40.900
they asked me if I wanted
to come home and man,

00:56:40.900 --> 00:56:42.360
we drove to that little house

00:56:42.360 --> 00:56:44.090
and I just threw all my shit.

00:56:44.090 --> 00:56:46.940
I grabbed shit left around
and threw it in my truck.

00:56:46.940 --> 00:56:50.773
And I followed them back home.

00:56:52.547 --> 00:56:56.350
And that's where I stayed with
them until I met my husband.

00:56:58.610 --> 00:57:01.910
If I hadn't gotten sick, I
probably would have stayed,

00:57:01.910 --> 00:57:06.910
truth be told for years,
and he took your power away.

00:57:08.618 --> 00:57:11.400
He took any choice you had away.

00:57:11.400 --> 00:57:15.110
There was no choice.

00:57:15.110 --> 00:57:18.450
And then, and I also felt

00:57:18.450 --> 00:57:21.350
like I had probably gone wrong somewhere

00:57:21.350 --> 00:57:24.240
and done something wrong by
continuing to speak to him

00:57:25.440 --> 00:57:30.260
when I was like 14 after
the whole kissing thing.

00:57:30.260 --> 00:57:32.390
And after all this shit,
when I was a little girl

00:57:32.390 --> 00:57:34.920
maybe I'd given him the signal,

00:57:34.920 --> 00:57:37.960
like a, oh it's okay, thing.

00:57:37.960 --> 00:57:41.788
Like maybe I had said

00:57:41.788 --> 00:57:44.100
or done something to make him think

00:57:44.100 --> 00:57:49.100
that I was okay with it or
that it was wanted or whatever

00:57:51.190 --> 00:57:52.960
but it very, very much wasn't.

00:57:52.960 --> 00:57:55.550
And I think it was very
obvious that it wasn't,

00:57:55.550 --> 00:57:59.713
from the first time that
he ever tried anything.

00:58:05.040 --> 00:58:10.040
I don't know why I couldn't
kind of fight him off,

00:58:10.950 --> 00:58:12.530
I fought back with my dad.

00:58:12.530 --> 00:58:14.350
I fought back with boyfriends.

00:58:14.350 --> 00:58:16.513
I fought back with my husband after.

00:58:19.000 --> 00:58:20.020
I'm not sure,

00:58:20.020 --> 00:58:25.020
but he definitely did
a good job of grooming

00:58:27.090 --> 00:58:31.230
also like from childhood onward,

00:58:31.230 --> 00:58:36.070
always, always there to say,

00:58:36.070 --> 00:58:37.700
no, there's nothing wrong with you

00:58:37.700 --> 00:58:39.010
and no, you're doing great.

00:58:39.010 --> 00:58:41.830
And I love you and I support you

00:58:41.830 --> 00:58:44.470
in whatever you do and answering the phone

00:58:44.470 --> 00:58:49.470
anytime I called and kind of
rushing in to save the day

00:58:50.140 --> 00:58:53.136
and sending me gifts

00:58:53.136 --> 00:58:57.400
and writing songs for me and about me

00:58:57.400 --> 00:58:59.570
and just doing anything you could to,

00:58:59.570 --> 00:59:01.610
like it was flattering.

00:59:01.610 --> 00:59:05.060
And I had never heard from a man

00:59:05.060 --> 00:59:09.990
in my entire life that I was beautiful

00:59:09.990 --> 00:59:11.810
or that I was a lady

00:59:11.810 --> 00:59:16.810
or that I could be
anything I wanted to be,

00:59:17.100 --> 00:59:19.450
even my good Pepo here in Tennessee.

00:59:19.450 --> 00:59:22.373
Like he was just different.

00:59:23.280 --> 00:59:25.990
He was my very best friend,
but a different breed of man.

00:59:25.990 --> 00:59:29.450
Like they just don't, here in my family,

00:59:29.450 --> 00:59:31.200
they just don't say things like that.

00:59:31.200 --> 00:59:32.680
So to hear that from him

00:59:35.490 --> 00:59:38.300
and to get the gifts
and to get the attention

00:59:38.300 --> 00:59:41.833
and to get all the things that I think

00:59:45.340 --> 00:59:47.873
he knew I was starving for,

00:59:53.440 --> 00:59:56.113
it was intoxicating, I don't know.

00:59:57.660 --> 00:59:59.740
And maybe that played a role in why

01:00:01.040 --> 01:00:03.683
I didn't say no because I could have,

01:00:08.950 --> 01:00:10.033
but I didn't.

01:00:15.420 --> 01:00:19.153
Told you it took me two
years to get my son back.

01:00:23.150 --> 01:00:26.613
It was a lot of trial and
error, methadone, suboxone,

01:00:28.950 --> 01:00:31.403
fucking up, falling off the wagon.

01:00:33.830 --> 01:00:38.787
Now I take benzos for sure.

01:00:44.150 --> 01:00:45.083
But that's it.

01:00:47.940 --> 01:00:49.280
You don't knock on wood.

01:00:56.000 --> 01:01:00.183
Some days, a lot of
days I want to get high,

01:01:05.710 --> 01:01:07.483
but I'm not.

01:01:13.840 --> 01:01:18.290
Losing my son for that couple of years

01:01:18.290 --> 01:01:20.820
and that even completely,
almost destroyed me.

01:01:20.820 --> 01:01:25.820
I can't imagine losing my girls and my son

01:01:27.490 --> 01:01:30.550
they're my world, I
would die if I lost them

01:01:31.523 --> 01:01:35.033
and trying to escape the girl's father.

01:01:37.620 --> 01:01:40.470
It's probably not a good idea
to go to court dirty, right?

01:01:40.470 --> 01:01:44.527
So I'm good right now, but who knows?

01:01:47.250 --> 01:01:51.403
People stay clean for
decades and then fuck it up.

01:01:54.860 --> 01:01:58.763
Secrets keep you sick, right? So.

01:02:15.640 --> 01:02:17.220
Thank you

01:02:17.220 --> 01:02:19.620
- [Mark] Took a lot of
courage for you to do this.

01:02:19.620 --> 01:02:21.120
- I appreciate it.

01:02:24.384 --> 01:02:25.484
Thank you very much.

01:02:25.484 --> 01:02:27.067
- [Mark] Thank you.

